{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>His father and his mother he curses.</b> To include after death (ibid.; Sanhedrin 5)." "<b>His blood is in him.</b> This is stoning. And so everywhere that דָּמָיו בּוֹ, דְּמֵיהֶם בָּם is said — we learn it from the ov and the yid'oni, about whom it is stated: בָּאֶבֶן יִרְגְּמוּ אֹתָם דְּמֵיהֶם בָּם (Sifra; Keritot 5). And the plain sense of the verse is like דָּמוֹ בְּרֹאשׁוֹ (Joshua 2) — he is not punished by his death other than he himself, for he brought it upon himself to be killed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:24.717824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}